Project Journal – Week of Sept 7–12, 2026
Project: Smart R2R Guide & Reparability Portal (RepairFlow)

Mon: Started on the system design diagrams – worked on the DFD context-level diagram (Level 0), mapping out how RepairFlow interacts with device owners, repair shop staff, platform admin, and the external LLM API.

Tue: Continued with the DFD set – Level 1 (core processes) and Level 2 (repair request and tracking flow), breaking down the components in more detail.

Wed: Group meeting to go over progress so far and align on the next set of diagrams and remaining work before the presentation.

Thu: Worked on the ER diagram – mapped out the main entities (users, shops, devices, repair requests, documentation embeddings, sustainability logs) and their relationships. Also did the use case diagram covering the three actors and their interactions.

Fri: Did the activity diagram for the core repair-request workflow, laid out as swimlanes across owner, system, and shop-staff, including the status/cost-update loop. Also touched briefly on some basic web frontend bits.

Sat: Reviewed the overall project direction and noted a few open ideas to carry into the next round of work.
